{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature Readings versus Intervals.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature Readings versus Intervals.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"temperature readings versus intervals temperature readings versus intervals","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature Readings versus Intervals.md","fileName":"Temperature Readings versus Intervals.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Temperature Readings versus Intervals","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Reciprocal Conversion Factors","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature Readings versus Intervals.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature Readings versus Intervals.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"temperature readings versus intervals temperature readings versus intervals","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature Readings versus Intervals.md","fileName":"Temperature Readings versus Intervals.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Temperature Readings versus Intervals","heading":"Temperature Readings versus Intervals","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An absolute temperature reading on the Fahrenheit scale requires both an offset and a scale change to become Celsius: Pryor's example uses $T_{\\mathrm C}=(T_{\\mathrm F}-32)/1.8$, taking 50 °F to 10 °C. A temperature difference does not need the 32-degree offset; an interval of 18 °F corresponds to 10 °C. The book also notes that one kelvin interval and one Celsius-degree interval are equal in size. Applying a multiplicative interval factor to an absolute reading therefore gives a wrong result. See [[Reciprocal Conversion Factors]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Reciprocal Conversion Factors","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature Readings versus Intervals.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature Readings versus Intervals.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"temperature readings versus intervals temperature readings versus intervals","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature Readings versus Intervals.md","fileName":"Temperature Readings versus Intervals.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Temperature Readings versus Intervals","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Engineering and Scientific Unit Conversions","Reciprocal Conversion Factors","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}